 the wire surface those\n9: //! answers drive:\n10: //!\n11: //! - **Anthropic**: explicit `cache_control` breakpoints with a\n12: //!   per-block `ttl` (\"5m\" | \"1h\"), a write premium (1.25× / 2.00×),\n13: //!   and read discounts. The tier choice is priced and must be placed\n14: //!   on the request markers.\n15: //! - **GPT/OpenAI**: automatic prefix-match caching — *no breakpoints,\n16: //!   no write premium* (per `docs/draft/codex-2034-review-20260610.md`\n17: //!   §48-55, haystack). The levers are `prompt_cache_key` (routing\n18: //!   affinity), retention (in-memory default vs 24h extended), prefix\n19: //!   layout discipline, and `cached_tokens` observability.\n20: //!\n21: //! # Equivalence discipline (flag-dark guarantee)\n22: //!\n23: //! When the resolved provider is Anthropic — the default — every code\n24: //! path through [`AnthropicPolicy`] is a pure delegation to the same\n25: //! functions the proxy called before this trait existed:\n26: //! [`write_policy::decide`] and [`TtlTier::wire_str`]. The tests at\n27: //! the bottom hold the backend to the →2032 decision table: identical\n28: //! `PolicyDecision` *and* identical post-call `LaneState` across the\n29: //! reference vectors. Anthropic wire bytes cannot change.\n30: //!\n31: //! # GPT skeleton status\n32: //!\n33: //! [`GptPolicy`] reuses the same lane machine: automatic prefix\n34: //! caching still rewards an append-only prefix and punishes mid-prefix\n35: //! churn, so WARM/DEAD classification and DEAD-path re-projection\n36: //! sizing carry over. The tier maps to *retention* instead of a\n37: //! breakpoint TTL. Wire-level field paths (Responses API vs chat\n38: //! completions) are pinned in A2 once codex capture data arrives —\n39: //! nothing here emits GPT wire bytes yet.\n40: //!\n41: //! →1985 binds both backends identically: a `Dead` decision licenses a\n42: //! faithful re-projection, never a truth-masking one, and usage-truth\n43: //! passthrough is not this module's to mo